
name: Gemini Read Only Code Audit

on:
  workflow_dispatch:

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  audit:
    name: Audit Y654 Project
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    timeout-minutes: 20

    steps:
      - name: Checkout Repository
        uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          persist-credentials: false

      - name: Gemini Code Audit
        uses: google-github-actions/run-gemini-cli@v0
        with:
          gemini_api_key: ${{ secrets.GEMINI_API_KEY }}
          prompt: |
            Act as a senior software architect.

            Perform a complete READ-ONLY audit
            of this entire Y654 repository.

            STRICT RULES:
            - Do not modify any files.
            - Do not delete any files.
            - Do not rename any files.
            - Do not create files.
            - Do not commit or push changes.
            - Only inspect, analyze and report.

            AUDIT THE FOLLOWING:

            1. List all existing files and folders.
            2. Find missing required files.
            3. Check Python syntax errors.
            4. Check broken imports.
            5. Check requirements.txt dependencies.
            6. Check backend architecture.
            7. Check API routes and endpoints.
            8. Check PostgreSQL configuration.
            9. Check database connections.
            10. Check Render deployment configuration.
            11. Check build and start commands.
            12. Check security issues.
            13. Identify missing tests.
            14. Check available tests where safe.

            FINAL REPORT:

            A. Project structure
            B. Existing files
            C. Missing files
            D. Critical errors
            E. Other problems
            F. Required corrections
            G. Suggested new files
            H. Backend readiness
            I. Render deployment readiness

            Give file paths and line numbers
            wherever possible.

            Clearly distinguish verified errors
            from possible problems.

            Never claim a test passed unless
            it was actually executed.

            Return the complete report in Markdown.
            
